        "original_id": "5f1b2b33-49c1-5046-aa10-5ca4714e38e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dziga Vertov, Frederic Zelnik, Lya Mara, Fred Louis Lerch, Stewart Rome\n- Roles: documentary film director, newsreel director, cinema theorist, producer-director, actor\n- Films: Lullaby (1937 film), The Crimson Circle (1929 film)\n- Topics: Soviet documentary film, German silent cinema, British-German crime film\n\nFacts:\n- Frederic Zelnik was born on 17 May 1885 and died on 29 November 1950.\n- Dziga Vertov was born David Abelevich Kaufman, was also known as Denis Kaufman, and lived from 2 January 1896 to 12 February 1954.\n- The Crimson Circle is a 1929 British-German crime film directed by Frederic Zelnik and starring Lya Mara, Fred Louis Lerch, and Stewart Rome.\n- Lullaby is a 1937 Soviet documentary film directed by Dziga Vertov.\n- Dziga Vertov was a Soviet pioneer documentary film director, newsreel director, and cinema theorist.\n- Frederic Zelnik was one of the most important producers-directors of German silent cinema and also appeared on screen as an actor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
